        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: அடிமை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அடிமை — aṭimai — \"a slave; slavery\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பழங்காலத்தில் பல பேர் அடிமைகளாக வாழ்ந்தார்கள். paḻaṅkālattil pala pēr aṭimaikaḷāka vāḻntārkaḷ. In ancient times many people lived as slaves."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also of a habit: பழக்கத்துக்கு அடிமை (aṭimai), a slave to a habit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அடிமை (aṭimai) is native Dravidian: DEDR 72 gives it under அடி, \"foot\", one who is at the feet of another."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
